From e2637a3e7505407c7255139a14829b2838fa03ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RushVR perf trace <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:51:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add a per-frame performance trace (perf_trace=1)

SHADPS4_PERF_TRACE=1 (perf_trace=1 in pc-vr\settings.txt) writes two CSV files into
pc-vr\user\log, independently of the log: perf_frames.csv, one row a presented frame (frame
time, the game's own CPU time, the GPU thread's CPU time, GPU time from Vulkan timestamp
queries, waits for the GPU, shader and pipeline compile time and counts, draws, passes,
submits), and perf_headset.csv, one row a headset refresh (new frame or repeated, xrWaitFrame
and xrEndFrame times). tools/perf-report.py sums them up and says what most likely limits the
frame rate (GPU, emulator CPU, game CPU, compile stutter, judder).

Also makes FrameStats::ThreadTime work on Windows (it returned 0), from the thread's cycle
count, so the GPU thread's CPU time is measured there too. Nothing changes while the variable
is not set.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018kCR2zyXAcmfP8xMfMVWtk
